  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1210 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nMain upper low will be crossing northern NM today, but with the\nrecent moisture and colder air aloft, we will see instability\nshowers and thunderstorms through the afternoon. Storms will be\nmoving and we are drying out so I don't think flooding will be an\nissue. Once the low moves into the Central Plains, it stalls out\nand we keep an elongated trough through eastern areas and a ridge\nbuilding into the Four Corners. This results in a Rex Block with \nour area in the NE flow side. This will bring back some low level \nmoisture and a cool front Thursday night. The NBM seemed pretty \nhigh for PoPs over far eastern areas, but with the easterly \nupslope flow, there will be low clouds moving in and especially \nover the eastern Sacs. Temperatures for most of the area will not \nget out of the 70s through the weekend. Easterly winds will get \nbreezy as well, with the focus on the western mountain slopes and \nout on the Lordsburg Playa. \n\nThe Rex Block breaks down by Monday as we start to feel the\neffects of the next upper trough moving in. The EC and GFS are in\ndecent agreement with this trough but the GFS is a little more\noptimistic with QPF amounts. NBM PoPs seem reasonable here with\nisolated to scattered coverage. Temperatures may be able to reach\n80 in the lower elevations early next week, but 70s still look\nwidespread.",
